# Nothing lands on main except by merging a reviewed pull request, and nothing rewrites it.
#
# Two definitions, both shared with a Claude Code hook so a session and a bare `git push`
# cannot disagree:
#
#   check-push-target.mjs   refuses any push that LANDS on main — also called by guard-bash
#   guard-push.mjs          refuses a force-push or delete OF main — the narrower rule that
#                           still bites under ALLOW_PUSH_TO_MAIN=1, because seeding main is a
#                           reason to append to it and never a reason to rewrite it
#
# git hands a pre-push hook one line per ref on stdin, and each script reads it, so the refs
# are captured once here and replayed to both.
#
# Client-side, therefore bypassable with --no-verify, and only present in clones where
# `npm install` has run. GitHub branch protection is the layer that is not; this is the fast
# one in front of it.
#
# Deliberate override for landing on main: ALLOW_PUSH_TO_MAIN=1 git push ...
refs=$(cat)

printf '%s\n' "$refs" | node .claude/scripts/check-push-target.mjs --pre-push || exit 1
printf '%s\n' "$refs" | node .claude/hooks/guard-push.mjs || exit 1
